# Trees 🌲

## Binary Search Tree (BST)

```python
class TreeNode:
    def __init__(self, val):
        self.val = val
        self.left = None
        self.right = None

class BST:
    def __init__(self):
        self.root = None

    def insert(self, val):  # O(log n) average
        if not self.root:
            self.root = TreeNode(val)
            return
        self._insert_recursive(self.root, val)

    def _insert_recursive(self, node, val):
        if val < node.val:
            if node.left:
                self._insert_recursive(node.left, val)
            else:
                node.left = TreeNode(val)
        else:
            if node.right:
                self._insert_recursive(node.right, val)
            else:
                node.right = TreeNode(val)
```

## Tree Traversals

```python
def inorder(node):    # Left, Root, Right (sorted!)
    if node:
        inorder(node.left)
        print(node.val)
        inorder(node.right)

def preorder(node):   # Root, Left, Right
    if node:
        print(node.val)
        preorder(node.left)
        preorder(node.right)

def postorder(node):  # Left, Right, Root
    if node:
        postorder(node.left)
        postorder(node.right)
        print(node.val)
```

> 🎯 **BST gives O(log n) search, insert, delete on average!**
